/// D30 (decided: escape once). A {placeholder} does not make a string's
/// backslashes go through escape processing a second time, so they print the
/// same with or without one; triple-quoted strings keep them verbatim.
x | 1
say("a\\\\b {x}")
say("a\\\\b")
say("""p="\\S" {x}""")
say("""p="\\S" """)
say("brace \\{x\\} and {x}")
